  "1. Ame-no-Uzume grants Miko's Bell to Phantom Thieves, providing them with buffs. When a Phantom Thief activates a Highlight or Theurgy, Miko's Bell will be transferred to them.\\n2. Ame-no-Uzume summons Ame-no-Uzume, and activates Dance at Ama-no-Iwato together with summoned Ame-no-Uzumes. Immediately afterward, Ame-no-Uzume will activate Founding Art, restoring HP based on the remaining HP of summoned Ame-no-Uzumes. Ame-no-Uzume will prioritize attacking Phantom Thieves with Miko's Bell, and inflict Kagura Dancer on targets.\\n3. When Ame-no-Uzume enters its second phase, it will transfer Miko's Bell to itself and become Frenzied, frequently spending its own HP to activate Frenzied Dance at Ama-no-Iwato on Phantom Thieves, dealing heavy damage. Additionally, Ame-no-Uzume's final damage dealt increases when attacking Phantom Thieves not in the Kagura Dancer state, and damage taken from these Thieves is greatly decreased. Having the Kagura Dancer state will nullify this effect.": "",
